{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "euclid-demo \u2014 a euclidean drum grid: repeatable structure, four independent layers.",
    "",
    "The 'grid' generator (euclidpercs) places each category with Bjorklund's",
    "algorithm, so every hit is decided by its own step index. That means the kick",
    "really does land on all four downbeats, every pass \u2014 the thing a Markov chain",
    "structurally cannot do.",
    "",
    "  kicks  X...X...X...X...   snares ....X.......X...",
    "  hats   X.x.X.x.X.x.X.x.   percs  ..x..x..X..x..x.",
    "",
    "The 'breathe' LFO rides grid.dropout, so hits thin out and return.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /grid                          print the grid (four rows, X = on the beat)",
    "  /grid preset=tresillo          fourfloor | backbeat | tresillo | bossa |",
    "                                 polyrhythm | sparse",
    "  /grid kicks=3 kicks_rotate=2   pulses and rotation, per category",
    "  /grid steps=12                 change the grid length; layers re-space",
    "  /grid dropout=0.5 8b           ramp the pattern open over 8 beats",
    "  /grid variation=1              spread hits across each category's samples",
    "",
    "preset= resets every pulse and rotation; individual settings win afterwards."
  ],
